.TH CRYPTSPACE 1 "September 2026" "Version 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cryptspace \- seamless LUKS volume mounter integrated with pass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cryptspace
[\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR|\fBstatus\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cryptspace
is a POSIX shell utility designed to securely attach, unlock, mount, and cleanly detach
LUKS-encrypted external drives or partitions. It integrates with \fBpass\fR(1) for
automated, keyless unlocking while guarding against accidental dirty unmounts.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B open
Unlock target LUKS device and mount it to the specified mount point.
.TP
.B close
Safely unmount filesystem and close dm-crypt mapper container.
.TP
.B status
Inspect status of dm-crypt mapper and current mount point.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-device \ path
Target disk block device or persistent path (e.g. \fI/dev/disk/by-id/...\fR).
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-mount \ path
Filesystem mount point path (default: \fI$HOME/workspace\fR).
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-pass \ entry
Password entry key stored in \fBpass\fR(1).
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-name \ name
dm-crypt device-mapper target name (default: \fIcryptspace\fR).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Per-machine configuration can be set in \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cryptspace/config\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Unlock and mount using defaults configured in config:
.IP
.nf
cryptspace open
.fi
.PP
Open an ad-hoc partition:
.IP
.nf
cryptspace open -d /dev/disk/by-id/usb-SSD-part1 -m /mnt/vault -p work/luks
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Crafted for sovereign POSIX environments.
